{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"f7ee2a4a03084a58d1d6d029a36a183aa3510117"},"timestamp":1561667614,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NjE3MzU3NDE=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3497","origin":"github"},"title":"using an s3 bucket as a common data source","message":"#### What is the problem?\nI am attempting to setup a cloud resource as a common data source for a git-annex repository as described in the Datalad [demo](https://www.datalad.org/for/data-publication). Instead of box.com I would like to use an s3 bucket. My attempts are failing.\n\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n\n```\n# Setup a datalad repo\ndatalad create demo\ncd demo\ndatalad run dd if=/dev/urandom of=big.dat bs=1000000 count=1  \ndatalad save\n\n# Setup a bucket for storing binaries (aws keys configured already)\nbucket=s3test\ngit annex initremote $bucket type=S3 chunk=1MiB encryption=none public=yes\n\n# while the demo uses url in the initremote command, here we have to get the public url separately\nurl=https://s3test-9f1339aa-49e4-4862-bf87-d99e6ecbe3b5.s3.amazonaws.com\ngit annex enableremote $bucket publicurl=$url\ndatalad create-sibling-github --publish-depends $bucket --access-protocol ssh s3annextest\ndatalad publish --to github --transfer-data all\n```\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using (run `datalad --version`)? On what operating system (consider running `datalad wtf`)?\ndatalad 0.12.0rc4 on OSX\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nI'm note sure what type of remote this is supposed to be but the error I get seems to be attempting to use the bucket as a git repository. The error given is:\n\nNo option 'url' in section: 'remote \"s3test\"' [configparser.py:get:792] (NoOptionError)\n\n[ERROR  ] Remote 's3test' has no refspec set.\n| You can set it as follows: 'git config --add \"remote.s3test.fetch +refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*\"'. [remote.py:_assert_refspec:747] (AssertionError)\n\nIt appears the above error can be avoided (though this may not be the correct path forward) by running the command:\n`git config --add remote.s3annextest.fetch '+refs/heads/*:refs/heads/*'`\n\nThis leads to the error:\n```\n [ERROR  ] Cmd('git') failed due to: exit code(128)\n |   cmdline: git -c receive.autogc=0 -c gc.auto=0 fetch --progress -v s3annextest\n |   stderr: 'fatal: repository 'https://s3annextest-de6985aa-e830-40bf-b43b-5991fdc9dabd.s3.amazonaws.com/' not found' [cmd.py:wait:415] (GitCommandError)\n```","files":null}]}